`,"scripts/tex-meadow.js":`// The meadow's grass, drawn in code: ONE script, one baked strip per query, every colour from lib/data/meadow.yml.
// Each strip is 512 px = 16 m of grass at 32 px a metre, FRAMES frames tall: the frames are the wind and the clip
// is "sway" (FPS frames a second, a seamless loop). A scene row wears a strip with sprite.repeatX and parallax
// [1, 1], so it reads as grass fixed to the world for as far as the player runs, at the cost of one sprite.
// The grass grows in clumps of curved, tapered blades over a solid dark body; in a clump the near blades are lighter.
// The wind is a wave: gust(x, f) says how hard it blows at x in frame f, and the crest travels down the strip.
// A blade bends most at its tip, and under the crest the tip catches the light.
// ?piece=back: the tall grass and its seed stalks, behind the player. (bare ref): the grass round the feet.
// ?piece=front: the short grass along the ground line, and dark clumps that pass in front of the player's shins.
// M.grass is the colour (root to tip), M.blades the density and height, M.plants the thin plants in the grass.
// A starting picture, yours to redraw or to write over whole.
import M from './lib/data/meadow.yml';
